   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Professions",
     "texto": [
      "To ask what someone does for work: **Che lavoro fai?** (what do you do for work?). With «Lei»: **Che lavoro fa?**",
      "You can answer in two ways: **Sono medico** (I'm a doctor) or **Faccio il medico** (literally «I do the doctor»). Both are normal.",
      "Many jobs change in the feminine: **infermiere** → **infermiera**, **cameriere** → **cameriera**, **studente** → **studentessa**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs ending in -are",
     "texto": [
      "Verbs ending in **-are**, like **lavorare** (to work), are conjugated in a very regular way.",
      "Two points to remember: the «tu» form ends in **-i** (lavor**i**), and the «noi» form ends in **-iamo** (lavor**iamo**).",
      "In the «loro» form (they), the stress moves back: **LA-vo-ra-no**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
